  "question": {
    "text": "Given a thin convex lens (refractive index $\\mu_2$ ), kept in a liquid (refractive index $\\mu_1, \\mu_1 \\lt \\mu_2$ ) having radii of curvatures $\\left|R_1\\right|$ and $\\left|R_2\\right|$. Its second surface is silver polished. Where should an object be placed on the optic axis so that a real and inverted image is formed at the same place?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "3mG55",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mu_1\\left|\\mathrm{R}_1\\right| \\cdot\\left|\\mathrm{R}_2\\right|}{\\mu_2\\left(\\left|\\mathrm{R}_1\\right|+\\left|\\mathrm{R}_2\\right|\\right)-\\mu_1\\left|\\mathrm{R}_2\\right|}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "MmqJQ",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mu_1\\left|\\mathrm{R}_1\\right| \\cdot\\left|\\mathrm{R}_2\\right|}{\\mu_2\\left(\\left|\\mathrm{R}_1\\right|+\\left|\\mathrm{R}_2\\right|\\right)-\\mu_1\\left|\\mathrm{R}_1\\right|}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "asDK5",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\left(\\mu_2+\\mu_1\\right)\\left|\\mathrm{R}_1\\right|}{\\left(\\mu_2-\\mu_1\\right)}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "qkIfE",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mu_1\\left|\\mathrm{R}_1\\right| \\cdot\\left|\\mathrm{R}_2\\right|}{\\mu_2\\left(2\\left|\\mathrm{R}_1\\right|+\\left|\\mathrm{R}_2\\right|\\right)-\\mu_1 \\sqrt{\\left|\\mathrm{R}_1\\right| \\cdot\\left|\\mathrm{R}_2\\right|}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/qumg3DA-ee55nbizFC7IxaeNCT3w0rctAPvgGXCTtWY.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n\n\n\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{f}_{\\mathrm{eq}}}=\\frac{2}{\\mathrm{f}_{\\mathrm{L}}}-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{f}_{\\mathrm{m}}} \\\\ & \\mathrm{f}_{\\mathrm{m}}=-\\frac{\\left|\\mathrm{R}_2\\right|}{2} \\\\ & \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{f}_{\\mathrm{L}}}=\\left(\\frac{\\mu_2}{\\mu_1}-1\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{R}_1}+\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{R}_2}\\right)\\end{aligned}$\n\n\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{f}_{\\mathrm{eq}}}=2\\left(\\frac{\\mu_2-\\mu_1}{\\mu_1}\\right)\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{R}_1+\\mathrm{R}_2}{\\mathrm{R}_1 \\mathrm{R}_2}\\right)+\\frac{2}{\\mathrm{R}_2} \\\\\n& =\\frac{2}{\\mathrm{R}_2}\\left[\\frac{\\left(\\mu_2-\\mu_1\\right)\\left(\\mathrm{R}_1+\\mathrm{R}_2\\right)+\\mu_1 \\mathrm{R}_1}{\\mu_1 \\mathrm{R}_1}\\right] \\\\\n& =\\frac{2}{\\mathrm{R}_2}\\left[\\frac{\\mu_2 \\mathrm{R}_1+\\mu_2 \\mathrm{R}_2-\\mu_1 \\mathrm{R}_1-\\mu_1 \\mathrm{R}_2+\\mu_1 \\mathrm{R}_1}{\\mu_1 \\mathrm{R}_1}\\right] \\\\\n& \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{f}_{\\mathrm{eq}}}=\\frac{2\\left[\\mu_2 \\mathrm{R}_1+\\mu_2 \\mathrm{R}_2-\\mu_1 \\mathrm{R}_2\\right]}{\\mu_1 \\mathrm{R}_1 \\mathrm{R}_2}\n\\end{aligned}$\n\nFor same size of image\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{u}=2 \\mathrm{f} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{u}=\\frac{\\mu_1 \\mathrm{R}_1 \\mathrm{R}_2}{\\mu_2 \\mathrm{R}_1+\\mu_2 \\mathrm{R}_2-\\mu_1 \\mathrm{R}_2}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
